# Webanyl Engineering, UX & QA Rules

## 1. Semantic HTML & Accessibility
- Use proper semantic landmarks (`<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<footer>`) and a single `<h1>` per page.
- Maintain high text contrast (WCAG AA minimum) across all surfaces and overlays.
- Every interactive control must have clear `:hover`, `:focus-visible`, and `:active` states.

## 2. Mobile-First Conversion Ergonomics
- Primary user goal on mobile is calling or requesting a quote within seconds.
- All tap targets (buttons, phone links, menu toggles) must be at least `44x44px`.
- Phone numbers must use clickable `href="tel:+420..."` links; addresses should link to maps.
- Input font sizes must be `>= 16px` to prevent unwanted iOS Safari zoom.

## 3. Images & Performance
- Enforce explicit `aspect-ratio` containers on all images to prevent Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS).
- Never use broken image URLs or watermarked stock previews. Use curated, high-resolution Unsplash/Pexels photos matching the Czech trade (or client assets in `_podklady`).
- Apply `loading="lazy"` to below-the-fold images and `fetchpriority="high"` to the main Hero visual.

## 4. Mandatory Automated Verification (Playwright CLI)
- Before finishing a build or major layout task, run the local dev server and verify the rendered page via Playwright (headless Chromium) at both Desktop (`1440x900`) and Mobile (`375x812`) viewports:
  1. Confirm zero horizontal overflow (`document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= window.innerWidth`).
  2. Confirm zero broken images (`img.complete && img.naturalWidth > 0`).
  3. Confirm zero uncaught console or page errors.
- Fix any detected layout or asset issues immediately before reporting completion.